<title>USA: USDA to close 2 US-Canada border ports of entry.</title>
<headline>USDA to close 2 US-Canada border ports of entry.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Agriculture Department said Friday that to cut costs, it planned to remove Champlain, N.Y., and Derby Line, Vt., as land border ports of entry for animals imported from Canada.</p>
<p>In a notice published in the Federal Register, USDA said it wanted to improve the efficiency of animal inspection operations along the U.S.-Canada border. The Champlain and Derby Line ports are currently open only part-time and have few imports entering the U.S. through them, the agency said.</p>
<p>Importers will be able to use other ports including Highgate Springs, Vt., and Buffalo and Alexandria Bay, N.Y., to import animals and animal germ plasm from Canada.</p>
<p>USDA said it would review comments from the public on its plan until Aug 26.</p>
<p>((Washington commodities desk 202 898 8467))</p>
